title: Socialisation in the Ruhr
subtitle: The miners want the pits for themselves.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 2 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1

= Socialisation in the Ruhr

In January a conference of the Ruhr workers' councils in Essen, with Social Democrats, Independents and Communists side by side, declared the coal mines socialised and elected a Commission of Nine to run them. The government in Berlin promised to consider it, then sent General von Watter and the Lichtschlag Freikorps to disarm the councils.

In mid-February the councils call a general strike. In Hamborn, Mülheim and the northern pits our people and the syndicalists lead it; in Bochum and Essen the Social Democrats are against. Watter's troops are already shooting.

- @arm: Spread the strike, and arm the pits.
- @councils: The councils take the mines and run them themselves.
- @nine: Stay with the Commission of Nine and the united councils.
- @organise: Use the strike to build the party in the pits.

@arm
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Left's answer. The Freikorps will make the Ruhr pay.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids armed action.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.ruhr_line = 1;
Q.militancy += 10;
Q.repression += 5;
Q.red_guards_strength += 1;
Q.red_guards_arms += 5;
Q.district_ruhr_members += 0.6;
Q.district_ruhr_loyalty += 5;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 8;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

In Bottrop and Hamborn armed miners fight the volunteers street by street. They lose, but the pits now know the party's name.

@councils
subtitle: The Left Radicals' answer, and the syndicalists'. Inspiring, and isolated.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids council action.
on-arrival: ruhr_line = 2; militancy += 6; repression += 5; district_ruhr_members += 0.5; district_ruhr_loyalty += 6; ultraleft_satisfaction += 8; lean_ultraleft += 2; unionist_satisfaction -= 4

Pit councils lock out the managers in a dozen mines and run the winding gear themselves. Within two weeks the troops have retaken them all, but the idea has spread.

@nine
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Right's answer: unity with the Social Democratic miners first.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids common work with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.ruhr_line = 3;
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.spd_relation += 4;
Q.uspd_relation += 4;
Q.district_ruhr_members += 0.3;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The Commission of Nine holds together a little longer. The strike ends without victory, but without a massacre, and the miners of every party have seen us keep our word.

@organise
subtitle: The Spartacist way: fewer heroics, more members.
on-arrival: ruhr_line = 4; worker_support += 2; district_ruhr_members += 0.8; district_ruhr_loyalty += 8; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 4; lean_luxemburgist += 1

Our organisers go from pit to pit with membership books. When the strike collapses, the new local groups stay.
